        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Craig Nicholls, Boy George, Rufus Wainwright, David Byrne, Josh Groban, Steven Page\n- Bands: The Vines\n- Songs: “Get Free”\n- Concerts: If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway\n\nFacts:\n- Boy George, born George Alan O'Dowd on 14 June 1961, is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Craig Robert Nicholls was born on 31 August 1977 and is an Australian musician.\n- Craig Nicholls is best known as the lead singer, songwriter, and guitarist of the Australian alternative rock band The Vines.\n- Craig Nicholls is the only mainstay member of The Vines.\n- Craig Nicholls, the frontman of The Vines, wrote the song “Get Free.”\n- The concert If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway featured men singing classic love songs to one another with a full orchestra.\n- If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway included performances by Rufus Wainwright and special guests Boy George, David Byrne, Josh Groban, and Steven Page.",
